course: dictionary
lesson: 3881
title: Reading road words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can belong to one place more than another. Freeway is mostly used in American and Australian English. Context helps you work it out: «A no pedestrians sign means nobody may walk there; you never walk on a motorway, freeway or highway, where cars drive very fast.»
explain: Look at the clues. Nobody walks there, and the cars drive very fast, so a freeway must be a road only for vehicles. Ask yourself what would fit: a big, fast road, not a path. Then test your meaning in the sentence. "You never walk on a big, fast road for cars" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Freeway, motorway and highway can all mean a fast road for cars. A child in London may say motorway where a child in Sydney says freeway. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A freeway is a big, fast road with several lanes in each direction.
fact: Traffic on a freeway does not stop at traffic lights or crossings.
fact: People never walk or ride bikes on a freeway; it is only for cars, buses and lorries.
fact: «Take the freeway» means drive onto the fast road, and a «freeway exit» is where you leave it.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and New Zealand, the same kind of road is called a motorway.
exercise: «You never walk on a freeway, where cars drive very fast.» Who uses a freeway? | Horses and riders | *Cars, buses and lorries | Children on scooters | Walkers and cyclists
exercise: A child in London says «motorway», and a child in Sydney says «freeway». What do they both mean? | A path through a park | Walkers and cyclists | A train line | *The same kind of big, fast road
exercise: «Take the freeway exit at the next junction.» Find and copy the word that tells you where to leave the road. | *exit | junction | take | next
test: «The freeway was crowded with cars and lorries, all driving fast.» What is a freeway? | A quiet lane in a park | Ababy path by the river | *A big, fast road for vehicles | A narrow track for bikes
test: Why must you never walk on a freeway? | *Because cars drive very fast there | Because the road is full of flowers | Because it has traffic lights every few metres | Because it is too narrow to see
exam: Which word means the same kind of road as a freeway in the UK? | *Motorway | Bridleway | Footpath | Pavement
